WEBVTT

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.950
"Ryoma Takebayashi"

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.570
Wow, time flies.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.570
--Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil,
I hope you are well.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.870
--Whoa, what a line!
--Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil,
I hope you are well.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.030
--Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil,
I hope you are well.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.120
--Welcome.
--Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil,
I hope you are well.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:19.990
--Well hello there, Manager.
--Dear Lady Eliaria Jamil,
I hope you are well.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.290
--Well hello there, Manager.
--It has been a short while since
I've left the care of your family

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.080
--I'm sorry we're keeping you waiting.
--It has been a short while since
I've left the care of your family

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.540
--It's fine.
--to live by myself
in the town of Gimul.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.250
--Good morning, Manager.
--to live by myself
in the town of Gimul.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.670
"Li Ling, Bamboo Forest Clerk & Bodyguard"

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.630
"Fei, Bamboo Forest Clerk & Bodyguard"

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.010
--Morning, Manager.
--Life out here is going well.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.510
Good morning. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.090
That's rare!

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:42.600
I was studying slimes
and lost track of time...

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.480
"Jane, Bamboo Forest Clerk"

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.980
Yes, we will take care of your laundry.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.690
"Fina, Bamboo Forest Clerk"

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.820
Next customer.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.320
Wow, it's so clean!

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.360
That's right!

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.660
"Maria, Bamboo Forest Clerk"

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.740
There's no dirt that
Bamboo Forest can't clean!

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.040
Manager, good morning.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.830
Good morning. Is everything all right?

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:06.790
Yes.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.380
You can count on us!

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.340
Thank you!

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.760
Good morning!

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.300
Oh, good morning, Manager!

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.850
"Selma, Bamboo Forest Head Cook"

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.850
Looking forward to another
productive day with you!

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.190
--Everyone is working very hard.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.940
--Good morning, Miss Carla, Mr. Callum.
--Everyone is working very hard.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.480
--As manager, I must provide
a proper work environment

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.190
"Carla, Bamboo Forest Assistant Manager"

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.940
--Good morning, Manager!
--As manager, I must provide
a proper work environment

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.900
--that is worthy of all their hard work.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.280
"Callum, Bamboo Forest Assistant Manager"

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.900
--Pleased to work with you today, as always.
--that is worthy of all their hard work.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.410
Good morning, everyone.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.740
Let's do our best today, as always!

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.910
Yes!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.960
"Episode 1"
"Ryoma and the New Plan"

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.470
Huh?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:28.600
I said, I would like for you to come to work
around this time every day.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:33.270
But why? We're always
so busy in the morning.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.980
Manager, when you come to work
before we open,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.150
you do all the preparation yourself.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.530
You're taking work away from
those who work under you.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.450
It's a good opportunity
to train the new workers.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.700
Additionally, it's a good
opportunity for you to learn

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.000
how to delegate and rely on others
to handle the work for you.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.250
I was taking work away from them...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.210
I understand. I'll do that, then.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.550
Also, I have a suggestion.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.640
Sure.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.100
About the second shop...

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.520
What's going on?

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.320
One moment, I'm almost done tying them up!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.900
Who are these people?

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.450
They're some thugs who came to complain
that we failed to clean their clothes.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.370
Huh? But what was all that laughter about?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.330
Well...

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.040
Hey, this is still so dirty!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.250
Look at all this dirt...

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.750
--Huh...?
--Clean...

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.760
I told you to make it so dirty
it'll never come off!

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.930
I did!

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.390
What a bunch of idiots.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.560
What did you say?!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.470
Who're you calling idiot?!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.230
--I'll go turn them in to the guards.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:57.600
--Damn it...
--I'll go turn them in to the guards.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.690
--Damn it...
--And that's what happened.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.320
--I'll remember this!
--And that's what happened.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.280
Huh...

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.150
What a nuisance.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.160
I did say, there's no dirt that
Bamboo Forest can't clean.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.950
Maybe I should give some more thought
to security around here.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.580
Glass...

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.620
Miss Carla!

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.000
Yes?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.880
There's something I want to try.
I'm heading back to the mines!

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.810
First, have the sticky slimes
make some hardening solution.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.570
Use the separation circle
to remove moisture.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.030
Add more hardening solution.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.830
Then mix with the mixture circle...

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.960
And remove moisture again.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:11.430
Repeat the process to condense
the hardening solution.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.230
Good. Now shape this into a sheet...

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.450
It won't break even when I hit it with
enhancement magic, and it's clear, too.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.540
It should work fine as
a replacement for window glass.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.500
It's hard enough to use
for security purposes.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.290
I should be able to protect
the workers and customers with this.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:48.090
Everyone, I want to make
lots of these. Can you do that?

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.890
That should be enough.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.570
I guess I should sleep now...

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.450
I've never seen this slime before.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.200
Appraisal.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:21.420
Medicine slime...
I don't remember contracting that.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.210
Did it evolve from something?

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.670
It has spear mastery as a skill.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.590
It must have been a poison slime before.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.390
But why did the poison slime
become a medicine slime...?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.600
I dropped a bottle of antidote yesterday.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.030
Oh, no! Dust cloth! Dust cloth!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.660
Huh?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:05.790
I thought the cleaner slimes
cleaned it up, but maybe...

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.670
Oh, they do indeed drink antidote.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:15.760
I guess poison slimes do indeed
evolve into medicine slimes.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.850
Meanwhile...

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.730
Can you show me what kind of
medicines you can make?

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.820
Quite a few, apparently.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.030
Appraisal.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:42.330
Ointment, hemostat, antidote...

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:46.460
Fast poison, slow poison,

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.130
fast paralysis poison, slow paralysis poison,

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.340
antibacterial medicine...

00:08:53.340 --> 00:09:00.350
Wow, how vast! I guess both medicines
and poisons count as drug synthesis.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.020
What is this "antibacterial medicine"?

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.520
"A fluid with strong
antibacterial properties.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.450
Kills off germs and viruses.
Harmless to humans."

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.450
Ah, a disinfectant!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.120
This might be useful.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:24.460
I'll do the things I can do,
one at a time.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.790
I have to make sure I don't
worry the Jamil ducal family,

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.960
who offered to be with me.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:38.800
Coming to think of it, I've been too busy
lately to catch up with the gods.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.850
I'll go to the church tomorrow!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:47.600
That kid is doing
interesting things again!

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.320
Pleased to be with you again!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:58.240
You're always on my mind,
Mr. Ryoma, every day!

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.790
Welcome, what brings you here today?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.870
Prayer.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:09.710
I see. This way please.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.670
Thank you.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:27.230
Huh? I thought I'd get sent to
the gods' realm like always, but nothing.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.110
I guess this is the actual normal outcome.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:42.830
This is like it usually is.
What was that weird delay?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:48.540
Sorry, I rarely use that power,
so I had to fumble around a bit.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:55.750
I've never met him,
but since he's here, he must be a...

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:01.340
Pleased to make your acquaintance.
I've started living in this town alone,

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.390
so I wanted to come and pay my respects.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:08.680
Yeah, I'm Tekun, god of technology
and craftsmanship.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.690
And you don't have to
bother with that polite talk.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.360
If I wanted to, I could read your mind.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.360
There's no point in trying to talk smooth.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.240
Besides, I don't like being formal.
Have a seat.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:28.250
All right, in that case, nice to meet you,
I'm Ryoma Takebayashi.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.870
Is that...

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.750
The one I made...

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:38.920
Yeah, I wanted to take a good look at it,
so I made a copy. Hope you don't mind.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.920
Like a replica, I guess.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.800
You're from Earth, right?

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.100
Yes.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.850
I was working in
a typical exploitative workplace,

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:54.900
and I died, rather easily,
from a sneeze while I was asleep.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:12:01.700
The gods picked me up and
reincarnated me into this world as a boy.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.700
Yeah, I heard.
Well, I did hear your story, but...

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.700
Techniques from another world
are really fascinating.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.170
Techniques? Even figurine making?

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:17.090
Items made by a foreign culture
using an unknown technique

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.460
are interesting to me, as god of
technology and craftsmanship.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.340
Because I'm a god,

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:27.850
I know all there is to know about
techniques from this world.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:31.810
So there are things you don't know
about techniques from other worlds,

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.850
which interests you.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.520
Exactly!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:40.440
Also, these figurines, it's obvious that
they were created with the utmost care.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.440
Although it doesn't appear
to be your main craft,

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:46.570
you did spend a significant amount
of time honing this craft, correct?

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.410
Making things was a hobby of mine.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:55.500
And to be blunt, sometimes I made good money
on these, through sales or commission.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.090
Since I was getting paid,
I couldn't slack off.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:04.430
Yeah, that's normal. But there are
many who don't think like that.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:09.140
As god of craftsmanship, I like people
who care about doing a good job.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:13.730
I see. By the way,
are you the only one here today?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.770
Yeah, the others just do their own thing.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.900
The God of Beasts, the God of Magic,
the God of the Earth...

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.530
This place must look like
just an empty white space to you,

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.490
but each god has their own spot
that feels good to be in.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:33.200
They build what humans would call
a house there, and live there.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:40.040
I see. I didn't know that.
So this is your house?

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:45.970
No, I don't have a house. I'm the god
of technology and craftsmanship.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:50.970
Technologies and crafts
exist all over the place.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.560
I just travel about, as I please.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.850
This place and the world
you live in are connected.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:04.110
Ask someone else for a better explanation,
I can't explain this well.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.990
I think Fernobelia would be
able to explain this better.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:12.620
Fernobelia? That's a name
I haven't heard yet.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:17.500
Oh, you don't know. He's the God of Magic.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.960
Fernobelia, God of Magic and Academics.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:26.090
He closes himself off in his realm.
I don't know what he does in there.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:30.510
But when it comes to knowledge,
he's the best, and he explains things well, too.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:36.350
He rarely speaks to anyone, though,
not even a fellow god like me.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.810
I don't know if you'll ever get to
meet him during your lifetime.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.570
So there are lots of types of gods.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.400
Yeah.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.700
Oh, it's time.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.200
I wanted to talk to you some more.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.490
I'll come again.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:54.740
Yeah, looking forward to it!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.340
Thank you.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:08.510
Thank you for your generous donation!

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.760
You're welcome. I'll come again.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.010
I guess it's all right to go to work now.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:22.270
I came in a little later than usual.
Is everything all right, though?

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.060
Perfectly fine!

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:28.240
The new workers have
learned their jobs pretty well.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.650
I see, that's good.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:35.580
So, Manager, I heard you
wanted to talk to us.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.370
Yes. It's about the windows in this shop.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.540
If someone wanted to
break in through there,

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.790
it would be pretty easy, right?

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:50.130
Yes, if they brought a hammer or axe,
it would be easy.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.840
We plan our security detail
with that in mind.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.180
Thank you for that.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.850
So I was thinking,

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:02.560
if we made the windows harder to break,
it would be easier to protect this place.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:08.570
This is something I'm thinking of using
as a replacement to glass windowpanes.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.860
It's very tough.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:19.700
Manager, can I give that a try?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:24.540
Of course, here. I have spares,
so it's all right if you break it.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.840
I'll hold it.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.930
Here I go!

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.600
Impressive.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.350
It won't budge.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.980
Did you make this, Manager?

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:42.810
Yes.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:46.440
This could be a very successful product.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:54.320
I'm sorry, but I don't intend to
sell these. It's hard to mass-produce.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.910
I see.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.870
I'm sorry.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.410
Li Ling, try the enhancement magic.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.160
Right!

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:15.430
This is indeed tough. If we use these
on the first floor windows,

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.430
it will certainly make it hard
for attackers to break in!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:22.980
But, if we're cornered,

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:26.650
we won't be able to break out
of a window to escape.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:31.650
I see, that is a drawback.
I didn't think of that.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.650
But it's very useful
for stopping intruders.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.120
We can replace some of
the windows with these

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:41.160
to decrease the number of
possible break-in points.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:44.410
If we know where they'll try to come in,
we can plan around it.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:49.840
I see. So is it all right if I replace
the store windows with these?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.130
Yes, please!

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.550
I'll start right away, then.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:18:00.050
Manager, didn't you have an appointment with
Mr. Serge from the Morgan Trading Company?

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.010
Oh, right!

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.310
We'll take care of this.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.180
Yes!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.190
Thank you, please do.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:11.360
Oh, Manager, I wanted to talk to you
about this yesterday.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.320
Yes?

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.940
It's about starting a second shop
in a different town.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:19.990
Ah... Yes, I think it's
still too soon for that.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.780
Is it?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:27.080
Since we have more manpower,
could you reconsider?

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.080
Understood, I'll think about it.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:36.510
I just started living by myself
here in the town of Gimul.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:41.720
It feels too early for me to
set up shop in a different town...

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:46.430
For now, I want to prioritize
the relationships I'm building

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.850
with the people I've met in this town.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.520
Welcome, Mr. Ryoma.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:56.110
Hello, Mr. Serge. I've come to do
some personal shopping today.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:59.660
I see. What do you need?

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.490
I want to purchase a large number
of bottles to store medicine.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.870
A large number, you say?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:10.830
Yes. I have some free time now,
so I wanted to make some medicine.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:16.630
Adventuring is prone to injury.
I want to be prepared for that.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:21.890
I see. But if you really want
a large number of bottles,

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:25.100
perhaps it would be best for you to register
as a chemist at the Merchant's Guild.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:30.890
Then, you can purchase them at a discount
from the wholesaler, through the Guild.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:38.110
I see, you came here
to buy medicine bottles.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:42.780
Yes, Mr. Serge suggested that I come here.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:46.330
So how good are you?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.620
Oh, of course.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.670
This is an antidote,
and this is a disinfectant.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.500
I see.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.630
You're pretty good.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:05.970
If you can make medicines such as these,
maybe you can live as a chemist, too.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.640
I don't plan to, at least not currently.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:14.060
Yes, right now your priority should be
starting up your second shop.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.860
--Huh?
--What is it?

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:21.280
Oh, um, it's just that Miss Carla, one of
the people who work for me, said the same thing.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.660
I think it's too soon, but...

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:28.540
I'm pretty sure you'd do fine
with a second shop.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.200
Really?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:34.920
Oh, if you don't have the funds
to start your second shop,

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.750
perhaps you could make
these drugs as a side business.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.970
I'll buy them all from you, if you'd like.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.300
What? All?

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.100
I have high hopes for you.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:58.110
I still think it's too soon
to start a second shop.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:03.700
Limour bird! It's a letter from Elia!

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:10.910
Mr. Ryoma, thank you for your letter!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:18.170
I have just finished my long journey home
and have finally settled down.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:21.300
My family is doing very well.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:26.260
The slimes we borrowed from you
are also doing well.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:37.400
Hearing about the hard work you're doing,
I feel as though I must do my best as well.

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:44.400
I wonder what I should do.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:48.200
It's about starting a second shop
in a different town.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:53.870
I'm pretty sure you'd do fine
with a second shop.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.210
A second shop...!

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:06.970
Elia, I think I'm going to get busy, too!
